{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Do not take from him.</b> For this is the proper way to sustain him — when you lend him without interest or increase." "<b>And your brother shall live with you.</b> This you shall do when your hand has enough for both yourself to live and to lend him, as they said, of blessed memory (Bava Metzi'a 62a): חַיֶּיךָ קוֹדְמִים לְחַיֵּי חֲבֵרְךָ (\"your life takes precedence over your fellow's life\")."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:59.886095130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}